  "readmeFile": "Readme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Release Notes and Important Information\n\n## Before You Update\n- Always back up your projects BEFORE updating.\n- This update improves SiticoneDataGridView with important fixes, smoother rendering, and new business-ready features.\n- Selection color behavior is now more reliable and consistent across rows.\n- The unwanted row auto-scroll on selection has been removed.\n- Rendering has been refined for a smoother and more stable experience.\n- New optional business features have been added and can be enabled only when needed.\n- Review the release notes BEFORE updating.\n- Contact support if you have questions BEFORE updating.\n\n## Improvements\n- Improved SiticoneDataGridView default appearance with a richer, more professional dark blue theme.\n- Added more beautiful built-in theme options for better visual variety.\n- Improved selection color consistency so custom selection colors behave correctly across rows.\n- Removed the unwanted automatic row jump when selecting rows.\n- Improved double-buffered rendering for a smoother experience.\n- Improved redraw handling to reduce visible UI disturbance during normal use.\n- Added row hover styling support for a more polished experience.\n- Added empty state support for cleaner presentation when no records are available.\n- Added column layout save and load support.\n- Added export support for CSV and delimited text.\n- Added clipboard support for copying selected content.\n- Added summary footer support for business data scenarios.\n- Added column format preset support for values such as currency, date, percentage, and numbers.\n- Added conditional formatting support for important business values.\n- Added status badge rendering support for columns such as Status and Payment Status.\n- Added built-in business context menu support.\n- Added row helper methods for common actions such as selecting the first row, last row, or a row by value.\n- Added more public properties and events grouped under Siticone-labelled categories for easier access in the designer.\n- Improved Smart Tag coverage for easier design-time configuration.\n\n## Compatibility\n- Designed to preserve backward compatibility for existing SiticoneDataGridView usage.\n- Existing public members remain supported.\n- New features are optional and can be enabled or disabled as needed.",
  "requireLicenseAcceptance": true,
